WEBVTT

00:01.640 --> 00:07.360
Masshiro na keshiki ni ima sasowarete

00:07.360 --> 00:13.400
Boku wa yuku yo mada minu sekai e

00:13.580 --> 00:14.660
Woah

00:19.340 --> 00:22.760
Maigo no mama tabi shiteita

00:22.760 --> 00:25.460
nezumiiro no sora no shita

00:25.460 --> 00:31.700
Higawari no chizu
ikutsumo no yume ga nijinde ita

00:31.700 --> 00:37.800
Itsuka wa sa chippoke na
boku no kono hohaba demo

00:37.800 --> 00:43.980
Ano kumo no mukou made yukeru kana

00:43.980 --> 00:50.000
Tsuyogatte kizutsuita kokoro sukashita you ni

00:50.140 --> 00:56.960
Furidashita amatsubutachi ga
ranhansha kurikaesu

00:57.060 --> 01:02.540
Massugu na hikari ga kousa shite

01:02.660 --> 01:09.140
Yukusaki mo tsugenu mama
dokomademo tsukinukeru

01:09.140 --> 01:14.900
Awai zanzou ryoume ni yakistukete

01:14.980 --> 01:21.100
Kono sora no shita donna toko ni ite mo

01:21.100 --> 01:28.100
Todoku hazu nanda mada minu sekai e

01:28.100 --> 01:30.920

01:46.600 --> 01:49.020
A smoke bomb and a grenade in one.

01:49.420 --> 01:52.300
That reckless fool is
beginning to annoy me.

01:52.300 --> 01:54.120
Do you think you can follow their scent?

01:54.120 --> 01:55.240
Uh-huh!

02:03.500 --> 02:04.480
Here, officer.

02:06.660 --> 02:08.620
Take her somewhere she'll be safe.

02:09.600 --> 02:13.300
Winry, Al is still
fighting, so I have to go.

02:13.820 --> 02:14.640
Okay?

02:15.440 --> 02:16.500
Okay? I'm sorry.

02:16.780 --> 02:19.220
When this is over, I'll explain everything.

02:31.560 --> 02:35.960
Why?
Why is waiting the only thing I can do?

02:37.600 --> 02:40.240
We have a girl in custody
in Sector 8 who appears

02:40.240 --> 02:42.100
to be a friend of the
Fullmetal Alchemist.

02:42.480 --> 02:46.120
Escort her to Central Command.
Repeat, Sector 8.

02:46.160 --> 02:48.920
We have a girl in custody who appears
to be a friend of the Fullmetal Alchemist...

02:48.920 --> 02:50.300
It's just about time.

02:50.300 --> 02:51.780
...Escort her to Central Command.

02:52.120 --> 02:53.300
Go and back them up.

02:53.320 --> 02:54.220
Right.

02:58.300 --> 03:00.300
There's a vacant house outside of town.

03:00.620 --> 03:02.300
That's where we'll meet up.

03:02.300 --> 03:03.580
Don't be followed.

03:03.580 --> 03:04.540
Okay.

03:05.660 --> 03:08.300
If something goes wrong, I'll let you know.

03:08.300 --> 03:09.300
All right.

03:13.680 --> 03:15.660
And Sir, please stay out of the field.

03:15.660 --> 03:17.400
I know, Lieutenant. Now go.

03:24.060 --> 03:25.300
You won't give up.

03:30.200 --> 03:32.140
This area looks deserted.

03:34.300 --> 03:36.000
A dead end. We're trapped.

03:39.900 --> 03:40.700
Hmm?

03:41.420 --> 03:42.620
Scar again.

03:43.380 --> 03:45.740
Gluttony, go see what he's up to this time.

03:46.080 --> 03:48.780
And I'll take care of our
two little friends here.

03:56.300 --> 03:57.300
What happened to me?

03:57.460 --> 03:58.300
What's wrong?

03:58.300 --> 04:00.300
My arm. My lord.

04:01.700 --> 04:03.300
I'm useless to you now.

04:03.760 --> 04:05.300
What are you talking about?

04:05.860 --> 04:08.040
You cannot burden yourself with me.

04:08.300 --> 04:10.300
If you do, they'll only get you too.

04:10.640 --> 04:13.020
A king is no king without his people,

04:13.020 --> 04:16.040
But a people without their
king would be lost as well.

04:16.300 --> 04:17.880
You can't do that to them.

04:18.100 --> 04:20.020
My lord, think of our clan!

04:20.160 --> 04:22.040
You must live for their sake.

04:22.200 --> 04:23.580
I won't leave you!

04:25.020 --> 04:27.780
Sometimes someone must be left behind.

04:28.540 --> 04:30.300
For the greater good.

04:31.380 --> 04:33.660
Lan Fan? What are you planning?!

04:33.780 --> 04:35.300
No! Don't do it!

04:37.980 --> 04:39.520
Watch out!

04:50.300 --> 04:53.080
There's nothing inside that armor.
You're hollow, aren't you?

04:53.520 --> 04:55.100
You poor boy.

04:55.300 --> 04:59.300
Alchemy trapped you in that metal prison
and yet you still have faith in it.

05:05.700 --> 05:09.800
True, there are plenty of things
about this body that are inconvenient.

05:09.900 --> 05:11.820
But it's nothing I can't live with.

05:11.840 --> 05:13.500
I don't need pity from anyone.

05:13.500 --> 05:15.080
Least of all from you.

05:15.540 --> 05:18.720
My brother used alchemy to save my life.

05:19.100 --> 05:23.060
To regret the form I have now would
mean not only rejecting alchemy,

05:23.060 --> 05:25.300
but also turning my back on him.

05:25.360 --> 05:28.040
I believe in my brother
and I believe in alchemy.

05:28.060 --> 05:29.480
I will not lose faith.

05:29.480 --> 05:30.900
I want to believe!

05:30.900 --> 05:32.100
Oh, do you?

05:42.940 --> 05:45.300
Brother, where's Winry?

05:45.300 --> 05:46.460
She's safe.

05:47.460 --> 05:48.960
No thanks to me, though.

05:49.060 --> 05:50.880
I made her cry again.

05:51.200 --> 05:53.860
You really should be more careful, brother.

05:56.660 --> 05:58.960
She doesn't like to
see you fight like that.

05:59.260 --> 06:00.140
Yeah.

06:01.640 --> 06:02.800
But she's gone now.

06:02.820 --> 06:04.060
Let's end this!

06:04.760 --> 06:06.960
Oh, I found you!

06:08.840 --> 06:11.400
The Ishvalan!

06:12.420 --> 06:13.760
You again.

06:14.000 --> 06:15.300
Look at his tattoo!

06:15.360 --> 06:16.500
Homunculus.

06:29.400 --> 06:30.400
Huh?

06:48.300 --> 06:49.480
It's Ling!

06:53.100 --> 06:54.800
Go! Move it!

07:00.860 --> 07:01.760
[GASP]

07:13.720 --> 07:15.300
Get me some strong cable.

07:15.300 --> 07:16.620
Right! On it!

07:20.080 --> 07:22.860
Your own regenerative ability
is working against you.

07:23.760 --> 07:25.720
Your flesh won't stop expanding .

07:25.720 --> 07:28.300
It'll keep you tied up nice and tight.

07:28.960 --> 07:30.300
You're mine now,

07:30.300 --> 07:32.300
Homunculus!

07:42.740 --> 07:44.800
That was well played, girl.

07:50.940 --> 07:52.880
I beat you.

07:56.360 --> 07:58.360
How does it feel to be tricked?

07:58.400 --> 08:00.020
You lose this round.

08:00.720 --> 08:01.840
What?

08:01.960 --> 08:04.060
That thing is a Homunculus?

08:13.120 --> 08:14.840
Put him in. We're getting out of here.

08:14.840 --> 08:15.620
Huh?

08:17.160 --> 08:18.160
Ah!

08:27.880 --> 08:29.580
Hold on a sec, Lieutenant.

08:29.580 --> 08:30.660
Shh!

08:33.720 --> 08:35.600
- Wait! What's going on?
- Al!

08:37.520 --> 08:38.920
The MPs are watching.

08:38.920 --> 08:40.360
Just pretend we don't know her.

08:40.940 --> 08:43.140
They're getting away! After them!

08:43.160 --> 08:43.840
Right!

08:43.860 --> 08:47.300
The Colonel may be a creep and a jerk,
but at least we can trust him.

08:47.680 --> 08:49.280
We have something to do.

08:59.960 --> 09:02.300
We have to get him, Al!

09:03.300 --> 09:06.220
You killed the Rockbells
and Nina, among many others!

09:06.300 --> 09:08.500
You're going to answer for your crimes!

09:18.380 --> 09:20.640
Are these two giving you trouble, servant?

09:21.060 --> 09:23.480
This is the servant of the
man who saved my life.

09:23.480 --> 09:26.060
You better leave him alone,
puny little boy!

09:26.060 --> 09:28.280
Wait a sec! Who are you calling puny?!

09:28.320 --> 09:29.880
Where'd that kid come from?

09:30.560 --> 09:32.760
Get away, girl. It's dangerous.

09:33.880 --> 09:35.700
They've got us outnumbered.

09:36.100 --> 09:38.180
It's time for us to retreat!

09:38.320 --> 09:39.120
Ha!

09:47.760 --> 09:50.000
Ah!

09:52.120 --> 09:55.020
[COUGHING]

09:56.440 --> 09:58.660
What kind of alchemy was that?

09:59.120 --> 10:00.900
She did it from that far away?

10:01.040 --> 10:02.280
Here, follow me.

10:05.380 --> 10:06.980
I can't see.

10:07.100 --> 10:09.040
Scar!

10:09.740 --> 10:12.820
[CAR HORN, TIRES SCREECHING]

10:13.560 --> 10:16.280
I know who you are, Ling Yao.
Don't worry.

10:16.540 --> 10:18.800
We're on our way to a secure safe house.

10:18.800 --> 10:20.860
My friend! I left her behind.

10:20.860 --> 10:21.760
Go get her!

10:21.760 --> 10:22.560
What?!

10:22.560 --> 10:24.520
No, we can't. We don't have time.

10:24.620 --> 10:27.340
Make time! She could be dying now.

10:27.340 --> 10:29.400
She's still waiting there for me!

10:31.080 --> 10:32.900
You had better make it quick.

10:36.700 --> 10:38.680
[CAR HORN]

10:39.200 --> 10:40.100
Huh?

10:44.540 --> 10:47.120
That woman driving...

10:47.120 --> 10:50.060
I'm sure she's Mustang's.

10:53.080 --> 10:56.300
I'm tired of playing
games with that upstart.

10:59.480 --> 11:02.300
Fullmetal Alchemist.

11:07.880 --> 11:11.240
Her eyes... Is that
how mine looked?

11:14.160 --> 11:18.680
No matter what I do,
hatred only breeds more hatred.

11:22.000 --> 11:25.300
There you go.
I think I managed to stop the bleeding.

11:25.520 --> 11:26.700
Thank you.

11:29.800 --> 11:32.840
Sir, the MPs are all closing in on us.

11:32.840 --> 11:34.380
We need to get going.

11:34.380 --> 11:35.900
He took a shot to the leg.

11:35.900 --> 11:38.080
In his condition,
he couldn't have gotten far.

11:38.080 --> 11:39.820
- Comb the area for him!
-[DOGS BARKING]

11:39.900 --> 11:40.580
Sir!

11:40.600 --> 11:42.500
Quickly, sir! Quickly!

11:43.400 --> 11:45.680
Xiao-Mei, where are you?

11:46.740 --> 11:47.900
Oh, no.

11:49.300 --> 11:51.080
Look what I found, Ed!

11:54.520 --> 11:57.580
We're a little busy right now
to be adopting panda bears, Al!

11:57.580 --> 12:00.720
I couldn't leave her alone in the
middle of all that mess back there!

12:00.720 --> 12:02.560
First stray cats and now this!

12:02.560 --> 12:05.600
Just how many animals can you
stuff into that armor of yours, huh?!

12:05.600 --> 12:06.500
Get rid of it!

12:06.500 --> 12:08.360
What a heartless thing to say!

12:08.520 --> 12:10.800
Look how sweet and gentle she is.

12:10.840 --> 12:12.360
[TINY GROWL]

12:13.920 --> 12:16.940
[GIGGLES]
It's all right, you're safe now.

12:29.480 --> 12:31.160
This way. Follow me.

12:31.160 --> 12:32.120
Thanks.

12:33.680 --> 12:35.860
You can stay in here, okay?

12:43.640 --> 12:45.300
Hey, Winry!

12:47.840 --> 12:48.620
Oh!

12:49.480 --> 12:51.300
Hello there, Fullmetal Alchemist.

12:51.760 --> 12:53.660
Fuhrer Bradley, this is a surprise.

12:53.720 --> 12:55.300
What brings you here?

12:55.400 --> 12:57.680
I heard that a childhood
friend of yours was

12:57.690 --> 13:00.300
under our protection here
at the Command Center.

13:00.840 --> 13:05.700
As a friend of such an important alchemist,
she deserves our every courtesy.

13:07.560 --> 13:09.280
I should be on my way now.

13:09.300 --> 13:11.300
If you'll please excuse me, miss.

13:11.500 --> 13:13.580
Oh, of course, sir.

13:17.960 --> 13:19.960
That's a nice, honest
friend you've got there.

13:19.980 --> 13:22.260
Make sure you both take good care of her.

13:30.600 --> 13:31.440
Ed?

13:31.620 --> 13:32.640
Huh?

13:33.300 --> 13:34.740
You promised.

13:34.900 --> 13:37.160
Tell me everything about my parents.

13:37.680 --> 13:39.120
What happened to them?

13:49.760 --> 13:51.480
I see.

13:51.680 --> 13:56.300
They did everything they could to
help others, right up until the end.

13:57.260 --> 13:59.060
But I...

13:59.180 --> 14:01.740
I just wish they could have
come back to me alive.

14:01.740 --> 14:03.560
Is that selfish?

14:05.560 --> 14:06.900
More waiting.

14:07.660 --> 14:09.980
That's all I can ever do.

14:24.320 --> 14:26.420
Ah, perfect timing.

14:26.480 --> 14:29.040
Miss Rockbell, there's
a telephone call for you.

14:29.680 --> 14:31.080
For me?

14:33.780 --> 14:35.160
Yes, hello?

14:36.060 --> 14:37.580
Oh, Mr. Garfiel!

14:37.600 --> 14:39.300
I'm sorry about this, Winry...

14:39.300 --> 14:43.360
I know you've got a lot going on,
and I tried to handle it myself, really.

14:43.360 --> 14:45.540
- Where is she?
- Isn't Winry back yet?

14:45.540 --> 14:47.920
Look at this!
Winry's the only one who can fix it.

14:47.920 --> 14:51.300
But I can't take this anymore,
your customers are so needy!

14:51.420 --> 14:54.420
Please hurry back, Winry! We miss you!

14:54.840 --> 14:56.540
You there, Miss Winry?

14:56.540 --> 14:57.480
Tetsu?

14:57.680 --> 14:59.640
Please come back to the shop soon.

15:00.080 --> 15:03.220
You do a much better job working
on my leg than Mr. Garfiel can!

15:03.220 --> 15:04.480
We need you here!

15:04.780 --> 15:06.580
Yeah, another thing, Winry,

15:06.580 --> 15:10.100
We still need an outer covering
for that model leg you made for me.

15:10.100 --> 15:12.860
- My arm needs work, too!
- Hey, hold on a sec! I was first!

15:12.860 --> 15:13.980
Miss you, Winry!

15:13.980 --> 15:16.940
You idiot, of course you miss her!
We all do.

15:16.940 --> 15:18.300
Isn't that the truth!

15:18.900 --> 15:20.200
I'm sorry.

15:20.720 --> 15:22.340
I'll be back home soon.

15:22.920 --> 15:24.240
Just hold on.

15:24.780 --> 15:26.740
I won't be much longer.

15:26.820 --> 15:28.460
I'll help everyone.

15:28.600 --> 15:30.360
Thank you all.

15:40.180 --> 15:43.120
Thank you both...
for stopping me back there.

15:44.700 --> 15:47.560
I forgot there were still
people who depended on me.

15:48.340 --> 15:51.800
If I had done it, I wouldn't have
been able to face them again.

15:53.160 --> 15:54.640
Of course.

15:56.580 --> 15:59.400
I expect you to take good
care of your auto mail.

15:59.520 --> 16:00.380
Yep.

16:00.520 --> 16:03.480
Oh, and I'll send you some
good polishing oil soon, Al.

16:03.540 --> 16:04.600
Great!

16:07.120 --> 16:08.900
And no dying, okay?

16:09.100 --> 16:10.380
Right.

16:11.780 --> 16:13.040
Oh, and...

16:13.320 --> 16:17.340
The next time I make you cry,
I hope that they'll be...[TRAIN WHISTLE]

16:17.360 --> 16:20.480
Huh? What?
I can't hear you!

16:22.540 --> 16:24.780
Brother? Wait up!

16:25.140 --> 16:26.560
See ya, Winry!

16:26.560 --> 16:28.480
Okay...jeez.

16:28.760 --> 16:30.300
Come back, Edward!

16:30.320 --> 16:32.200
What were you saying?

16:36.680 --> 16:39.880
The next time I make you cry,
I hope they'll be tears of joy!

16:39.880 --> 16:42.320
Then Al and I will be
back in our normal bodies,

16:42.320 --> 16:44.960
and I'll make you cry
out of sheer happiness!

16:45.020 --> 16:46.260
That's a promise!

16:46.260 --> 16:49.480
[LAUGHS]

17:01.100 --> 17:03.120
Give me a new arm and a leg.

17:03.680 --> 17:05.320
I need one year.

17:05.320 --> 17:06.560
Well...

17:06.820 --> 17:09.280
There's no turning
back for us now, brother.

17:12.220 --> 17:14.600
What are you crying for, Winry?

17:33.660 --> 17:36.980
All this time...have I been...

17:36.980 --> 17:38.980
Falling for him?

17:46.880 --> 17:48.080
Colonel!

17:48.180 --> 17:49.700
Get in the car.

17:57.480 --> 18:00.820
Someone's badly injured.
I came to you because we need a doctor.

18:01.600 --> 18:05.300
Got yourself in trouble again.
Just can't help yourself.

18:05.300 --> 18:08.480
I know you have a family.
I wouldn't want to endanger them.

18:08.520 --> 18:11.060
If you'd rather not get
involved, I'll understand.

18:12.260 --> 18:14.800
Wait here. I'll get my instruments.

18:14.900 --> 18:16.440
You sure about this?

18:18.300 --> 18:22.300
My wife and I split up not long
after I came back from duty in Ishval.

18:24.600 --> 18:27.700
You let her wander around
the sewers with her arm cut off?

18:27.820 --> 18:30.020
Don't blame me if she gets lockjaw.

18:32.480 --> 18:36.000
I'm afraid the only patients
I've had lately have been corpses,

18:36.000 --> 18:38.100
so this might be a little rough.

18:41.000 --> 18:44.900
[LAN FAN SCREAMING]

18:45.540 --> 18:47.420
- I'm sorry—
- No, don't apologize.

18:48.400 --> 18:50.860
I'm the one who suggested it, remember?

18:51.240 --> 18:54.300
We both had something to
gain out of it, so it made sense.

18:54.720 --> 18:56.900
When I went in search of immortality,

18:57.040 --> 19:00.240
I knew I must be ready
to make certain sacrifices.

19:03.040 --> 19:04.840
But I...

19:05.060 --> 19:07.220
I wasn't ready for this.

19:08.580 --> 19:09.980
Lan Fan was, though.

19:09.980 --> 19:12.820
She made the decision
that I was too weak to make.

19:15.100 --> 19:18.220
[WHIMPERING]

19:19.180 --> 19:21.180
[GASPS]
She's awake!

19:21.200 --> 19:23.620
You okay? Is there anything we can do?

19:25.120 --> 19:28.620
That old trap of yours worked pretty well.

19:31.460 --> 19:33.620
But I'm useless without my arm.

19:34.020 --> 19:36.300
I'm going to need to find a replacement.

19:38.800 --> 19:42.880
You know, I can introduce
you to a great engineer.

19:50.300 --> 19:52.020
I'm with the state military.

19:52.180 --> 19:53.840
Name's Colonel Roy Mustang.

19:55.940 --> 19:59.300
And my name is Ling Yao,
the twelfth son of the Emperor of Xing.

19:59.680 --> 20:01.940
I appreciate you finding a doctor.

20:02.300 --> 20:03.460
It was no problem.

20:03.460 --> 20:05.840
Thank you for helping
us with the Ross incident.

20:06.500 --> 20:09.860
And also...
for bringing this thing in.

20:14.500 --> 20:16.660
Hey, what do we have here?

20:17.100 --> 20:19.860
That's Gluttony. He's a Homunculus.

20:21.960 --> 20:23.980
He and his friends
appear to have connections

20:23.980 --> 20:26.380
among some of the
military's senior staff.

20:26.380 --> 20:27.300
[GASP]

20:27.300 --> 20:30.060
Just some, you say?
It goes far deeper than that.

20:31.180 --> 20:32.860
Your Führer King Bradley?

20:32.860 --> 20:35.560
I believe it's possible that
he's a Homunculus too.

20:35.560 --> 20:36.880
[GASPS]

20:37.300 --> 20:38.780
I saw his eye.

20:38.780 --> 20:41.680
The one under the patch,
it had an Ouroboros tattoo.

20:41.680 --> 20:44.940
He and Gluttony came after us
and they were working together.

20:45.060 --> 20:46.080
No way!

20:46.280 --> 20:48.680
Our ruler? A Homunculus?

20:48.720 --> 20:50.680
Although...

20:50.980 --> 20:55.220
Bradley doesn't have the same sort of
inhuman presence that you get from Gluttony.

20:55.520 --> 20:58.420
At his core, he still feels
like a regular person.

20:58.440 --> 21:03.080
Another thing, if the Führer is a
Homunculus, how can he possibly have a son?

21:03.500 --> 21:07.300
It's said in that book that the Homunculi
have no reproductive capabilities.

21:07.400 --> 21:11.220
No, the Führer's son Selim is adopted.

21:11.220 --> 21:14.300
There's no direct blood relation
between him and his father.

21:17.200 --> 21:18.480
[ROY SCOFFS]
AL: Huh?

21:18.580 --> 21:20.600
Whether he's monster or human,

21:20.780 --> 21:25.280
either way, these new developments will make
it easier to remove him from the seat of power.

21:26.100 --> 21:28.480
First, we get information out of this one.

21:28.680 --> 21:30.180
And I'll take his stone.

21:30.280 --> 21:32.700
It may prove useful in treating my man.

21:33.040 --> 21:34.320
Hey, you!

21:34.320 --> 21:36.580
Lan Fan lost her arm to get him!

21:36.620 --> 21:39.340
He's our captive!
We're taking him back to Xing!

21:39.460 --> 21:41.840
Hold it!
He could help us get our bodies back!

21:41.920 --> 21:44.020
We've been working on that for a long time.

21:44.120 --> 21:46.300
I'm not gonna let you
just waltz off with him!

21:46.300 --> 21:49.080
That's right!
Think about it, Ling.

21:49.200 --> 21:50.460
You're an illegal alien!

21:50.480 --> 21:52.060
I'm too old for this kind of thing.

21:52.080 --> 21:54.620
Good luck, Mustang. I'm going home.

21:54.620 --> 21:55.220
Listen to me...

21:55.240 --> 21:56.620
Colonel Mustang.

21:57.700 --> 21:59.960
Mustang was one who killed Lust.

22:00.060 --> 22:02.940
Mustang must pay for what he did to her!

22:10.580 --> 22:13.300
Roy Mustang!

22:24.940 --> 22:26.300
What was that?!

22:28.860 --> 22:34.320
Let it all out, let it all out

22:34.320 --> 22:38.760
Tsuyogaranakute ii n da ne

22:39.760 --> 22:45.100
Dareka ga kaite'tta

22:45.100 --> 22:51.120
Kabe no rakugaki no hana ga yureru

22:51.580 --> 22:56.680
Jibunrashisa nante, dare mo wakaranai yo

22:56.680 --> 23:02.200
Nagai nagai michi no tochuu
de nakushitari, hirottari, 

23:02.520 --> 23:11.960
Kyuu ni samishiku natte,
naichau hi mo aru kedo

23:12.100 --> 23:17.580
Namida mo itami mo, hoshi ni kaeyou

23:17.580 --> 23:23.480
Ashita wo terasu akari wo tomosou

23:23.540 --> 23:31.540
Chiisana te kazashite
futari de tsukurou hoshikuzu wo

23:31.540 --> 23:33.820
Tsuyoku hikaru ein wo

23:33.920 --> 23:39.340
Sayonara itsuka wa kuru ka mo shirenu

23:39.340 --> 23:45.560
Kisetsu wa sore demo meguri megutte'ku

23:45.560 --> 23:53.200
Chiisaku mayotte mo aruite'ku
Kimi to aruite'ku

23:53.440 --> 23:57.740
Sore daku wa kawaranaide iyou ne

23:59.800 --> 24:02.920
What lies safely hidden behind lying eyes?

24:03.220 --> 24:06.280
Behind fake smiles,
and feigned friendship?

24:06.620 --> 24:09.220
Finding out will be no easy task.

24:09.400 --> 24:13.840
Enter the forest, grope in
the darkness for the unknown.

24:14.120 --> 24:17.380
Next time on Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

24:17.640 --> 24:21.120
Episode 24: Inside the Belly

24:21.580 --> 24:23.300
If you move carelessly...

24:23.320 --> 24:28.180
Nothing but pain will await
you in the inky blackness.
